# fixedbugs, defect 360, lane cli12, 2026-10-05.
#
# Beside `fixedbugs-360-a-header-that-does-not-compile`: the same header
# also refutes the extern, `-> i32` over `int64_t`. clang reads on past an
# error, and what it says after one about a header it could not read whole is
# no verdict on the declarations checked against it, so the header is told
# alone, on its string, and the extern is checked once the header compiles.
# Before this repair the extern's `ffi_return_type` was told and the header's
# error left unsaid, a second build away.

extern "fixedbugs-360-refuted.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function six() -> i32

function main()
    print(six())
